Z||000000||mlmpetert||01-25-2001||09:44 PM||||I have a 86 gt and want to do a rear brake conversion. I hear that you use front calipers and rotors form a grand am. But im not sure how to do it and dont know what other parts are needed and what year grand am. And also how do i put the emergency cable on front wheel calipers?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||01-25-2001||09:48 PM||||You should be able to find all the info you need about the Grand Am brake upgrade at <A HREF="http://fierozone.tripod.com/frontpage/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierozone.tripod.com/frontpage/index.html</A> <P>Note that you loose the e-brake when you do this upgrade.  For this reason I cannot do this on my car because of the NC inspection requirements.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||RaeQwan||01-26-2001||02:03 AM||||Bob, its odd you should say that bout the NC requirements, my ebrake doesn't work.. I have pieces missing & broke(hehe), which I will eventually look into replacing... but I've never had the guy even LOOK at my brakes, just the lights and horn and thats bout is..<P>------------------<BR>Ray - AIM: WookieeNC<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Fiero Coupe</A> - <A HREF="http://www.CarolinaFieros.com" TARGET=_blank>Carolina Fieros</A> - <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/dearabu/" TARGET=_blank>Dear Abu</A> - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.net" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Network</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||01-26-2001||08:53 PM||||You might also want to review the thread on brake math. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007762.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007762.html</A>  there is a bunch of data in that thread.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bob Englert||01-26-2001||09:30 PM||||Ray:<P>Consider yourself lucky that you take your car to someone that doesn't to a proper inspection.  The ebrake is supposed to be checked when it is inspected.<P>I will be posting a location for our Feb 3rd Fiero meeting in Raleigh by Sunday.  I will be in Raleigh on Satuday on business and I will look for a location that can take 15-20 people.  We plan to meet at about 2:00PM.<P>Hope to be able to meet you then.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
